Backport of llvm/llvm-project 905a88b923 (#198129) to lld 21.1.8, plus
used(false), since 21.x still has Symbol::used and relied on the same
memset to zero it.

makeDefined and initSectionsAndLocalSyms memset the storage and then
placement-new a Symbol into it. The new object's lifetime begins at the
placement new, so GCC's lifetime DSE may drop the memset. GCC 16 does,
leaving Symbol::flags and partition uninitialized, and `ld -r` then
writes STT_SECTION symbols with st_shndx SHN_UNDEF (ClangBuiltLinux/linux#2162).

